      "content": "Serving large language models efficiently in production is rarely a matter of picking default configurations from engine documentation. Engine settings that deliver high throughput on an A100 often degrade under different prompt distributions or hardware setups.\n\nRigtune automates the empirical search for optimal serving configurations across engines like vLLM, SGLang, and llama.cpp. Rather than guessing parameters, it benchmarks combinations of quantization precisions, key-value cache strategies, and speculative decoding against your specific traffic patterns. On workloads testing models like Qwen and Gemma, this benchmark-driven tuning yielded throughput gains of 1.5 to 1.8 times over standard configurations while maintaining output accuracy on GSM8K evaluations.\n\nOnce profiling finishes, the tool serves the winning configuration behind a unified, OpenAI-compatible endpoint. This eliminates the manual guesswork usually required when deploying custom inference workloads."
