      "content": "Autonomous coding agents frequently degrade software systems because they lack memory of historical design intent and architectural trade-offs discussed in previous conversations.\n\nKibi addresses this continuity problem by embedding a formal requirements framework directly inside the repository. Using a bundled SWI-Prolog runtime connected through the Model Context Protocol, it captures requirements, assumptions, and validation rules as declarative knowledge rather than transient conversational context.\n\nBefore modifying code, the agent queries the knowledge base to inspect existing constraints. When an agent proposes a change that violates an earlier architectural rule, the logic engine flags the direct contradiction and halts execution. It also verifies that each business requirement maps directly to automated regression suites.\n\nShifting agent management from loose prompt engineering to structured formal logic verification prevents long-term codebase erosion."
